 "_doc": "REPO-SHAPE-1 (Rowan, 2026-11-26): a change of 3,000 files and 291,031 added lines is unreviewable and unsustainable, and a repository that holds code, state and generated evidence in one tree cannot be maintained by the system that writes it. Read by foundation/reposhape.py. A path belongs to the area with the longest matching prefix (path '.' is a file at the root). class says how fast it changes and who owns it: kernel (the code every system runs, published to ultrastable/seed), platform (builds and runs Ultrastable itself), docs (prose and specifications), assets (brand and media), state (queue items, ledgers, evidence, packets: written by loops, never by a session, and leaving git for D1, R2 and the evidence branches). mode: here (lives in this repository), moving (a move is under way, nothing is deleted until the destination runs the consumer). The size of a change is gated once, by SMALL-CHANGE-1 (size_gate); `foundation reposhape --split` writes the stack of in-budget branches that carries an oversize branch's tree and leaves the original untouched.",
